WEBVTT

00:07:28.907 --> 00:07:30.851
before was better.

00:07:33.793 --> 00:07:36.103
A few months after I got sick,
I wrote about this

00:07:36.127 --> 00:07:39.106
and then I sent it off to an editor
at the "New York Times."

00:07:39.742 --> 00:07:43.939
In retrospect, taking one of the most
vulnerable moments of your life

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.493
and turning into an op-ed

00:07:45.517 --> 00:07:48.307
is not an amazing way
to feel less vulnerable.

00:07:48.331 --> 00:07:49.817
(Laughter)

00:07:49.841 --> 00:07:52.616
I got thousands of letters and emails.

00:07:52.943 --> 00:07:54.496
I still get them every day.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.901
I think it is because
of the questions I asked.

00:07:58.321 --> 00:08:02.921
I asked: How do you live
without quite so many reasons